; Jets: 9 along ribs (X, 3.0 mm, die 27.0 mm exact) x 12 along the return-slot
; long axis (Y, 2.4 mm) = 108 per die, N=216.
; Cell row Y = 28.8 mm, 0.8 mm wider than the 28 mm die.
; Plate envelope in Y = 28+1.2 = 29.2 mm, so 0.4 mm remains inside the envelope.
; q''_nominal = (858/216)/(2.4e-3*3.0e-3) = 551697.5308641976 W/m2 = 55.16975308641976 W/cm2.
; Applied BC is 1.05 x nominal (edge-hole / nonuniform redundancy). Flow is NOT scaled.
; q''_BC = 579282.4074074075 W/m2 = 57.92824074074075 W/cm2.
; Coupon power at the BC = 858*1.05 = 900.9 W. Plate spec stays 429+429+198+44 = 1100 W.
; Die-average flux stays 429/(27*28 mm2) = 56.74603174603175 W/cm2. That is not the coupon BC.
; mdot = (992.2*1.60/60000)/216 = 0.00012249382716049385 kg/s. Tin=313.15 K. D=0.40 mm unchanged.
